description:
Implement COVERAGE-MATRIX.md §3 exactly.

Migration 0002 is hand-written DDL like 0001. It adds:
- the shared trigger function kidsphere_append_only;
- 6 tables, each with its guard trigger: ai_suggestions, record_versions, teacher_assessments (one open cycle and one initial cycle per child), teacher_assessment_entries (13-domain CHECK; inserts only into an open cycle), functional_summaries (only the draft→approved update is allowed), report_exports;
- focus_areas.follow_up_on, assessment_id and source_need, plus a DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED constraint trigger that allows at most 3 active focus areas;
- observations.domains (text[] with a CHECK against the 12 AI domains, GIN index) and observations.attributes;
- development_reviews.follow_up and ai_suggestion_id;
- generated_content.deleted_at and deleted_by, with a CHECK that only drafts can be soft-deleted.

Data steps inside the migration (§3.4), all idempotent:
- record_versions seq-1 backfill rows for every existing profile section (via jsonb_each), observation, focus area and non-archived content row;
- observations.domains backfilled from area;
- focus_areas.follow_up_on parsed from plan.review_on;
- a Python step that adds only the parent_perspective.questionnaire and per-perspective section_status keys when they are absent.

The downgrade drops only new objects.

Application code:
- models.py mirrors the migration with 6 new classes and the new columns.
- services/history.py: record(db, *, child_id, entity_type, entity_id=None, key='', data, user, reported_by=None, via, review_id=None, ai_suggestion_id=None) with seq = max+1, and versions(db, ...).
- app/provenance.py: a pure derive() returning parent_said, teacher_observed, ai_suggested or teacher_approved (§3.3.4).
- vocab.py merges list fragments from app/data/lists/*.json into the options lists, so wave-2 packages never edit options.json. common.json holds section_statuses, provenance, ai_domains (12), observation_domains (13 assessment sections), yes_no and yes_no_sometimes, all labelled en/ar/he.

Edits to options.json:
- contact_preferences gains 'other'; the he label of 'meeting' becomes 'פגישה מסודרת';
- independence_areas gains organizing_belongings; dressing is relabelled 'Dressing / undressing';
- the he label of hope_child_feels.safe becomes 'בטוח/ה';
- new banned_terms.ai_only group (referral wording, en/he/ar);
- allow_phrases gains the exact 3 PDF disclaimer sentences.

Also:
- errors.py gains ASSESSMENT_OPEN, ASSESSMENT_CLOSED, SUMMARY_APPROVED, REPORT_BUSY and REPORT_FAILED.
- routers/source_model.py serves GET /api/source-model from app/data/source/*.json, tolerating missing files until wave 2 adds them.
- docs/terminology.md records the OQ-3 label decisions.

Run tests only on the Ubuntu server with deploy/ci/remote-test.sh.

Implement every PQ-* row of the matrix (§2.1) plus X-02, X-03, X-05 (profile part), X-06, X-07 and X-10.

Registry: create backend/app/data/source/parent_questionnaire.json, containing every PQ-* and PQ-SEC-* id. Each entry has section, order, kind, storage path, option list, sensitivity (none/third_party/family/health/medical), ai_policy (never/label/domain), PDF section, labels in en/ar/he and the verbatim source_he. It also holds the maps_to data for the legacy projection. The list fragment lists/parent_questionnaire.json adds pq_interests, pq_frustration_reactions, pq_morning_separation, pq_social_contact, pq_express_needs, pq_degree, pq_stop_activity and health_food_flags.

Backend:
- Extend schemas/profile.py with the new sections and keys (§3.3.1): joy, separation, communication, health, behaviour, transitions, expectations, partnership, heart, plus bridge on the teacher perspective; not_answered validated against the section fields; text answers up to 4000.
- Extend services/profiles.update_profile:
  - section status;
  - questionnaire metadata and submit;
  - entered stamps with mode;
  - the legacy projection in questionnaire_projection.py (§3.3.2), including the union into children.additional_languages;
  - one history.record() per changed section;
  - compute_lists reads bridge.main_strengths (main:true) and calms_helps;
  - profile_out exposes provenance[] from app.provenance.
- Rules: exactly 3 main strengths when the bridge status is sufficient. Parents never see the teacher perspective or bridge, and get 403 when writing it.
- New endpoint GET /api/children/{id}/profile/history (staff only).

Frontend:
- The parent wizard becomes PW1–PW9 in source order (§5.2), with skip links, conditional follow-ups, privacy notices on PW6 and PW8, and Send on PW9.
- Staff use the same flow in on_behalf and meeting modes from the Parent View. Replace the per-step Parent/Teacher toggle in the staff wizard.
- The Parent View tab (features/parent-view) renders the registry in source order, with statuses, Not answered markers, Private badges on health and family, a history drawer, an Initial/Latest toggle and a 'From the earlier form' block.
- The Quick Baseline page (features/quick-baseline) is one screen (§5.4) with a Create baseline call to action.
- The parent home (features/parent) shows the questionnaire status and a continue link.

Implement every OM-D00..D14 row and OM-LEVEL of the matrix (§2.2), plus X-04, X-08, X-11, X-13, X-36 and X-37.

Registry: create backend/app/data/source/observation_model.json, containing every OM-* id. Each entry has domain key, subgroup, item key, kind, storage path, ai_domain (D03-11..14 → communication), sensitivity, ai_policy, PDF section, labels in en/ar/he (KidSphere wording per terminology.md and OQ-3) and the verbatim source_he, which is never rendered. The list fragment lists/observation_model.json adds observation_principles (7), observation_frequency, sensory_effects and need_areas (11, with maps_to priority_categories).

Backend:
- schemas/assessments.py defines one StrictModel per domain (§3.3.5).
- services and routers implement §4.2:
  - cycles: create, header patch, close, and reassessment with copy_forward;
  - PUT /domains/{d} appends an entry, refreshes the teacher_assessments.domains cache and returns warnings, including a soft warning when strengths are below 3;
  - per-domain history;
  - apply, which merges into CPL with source observation and a via field;
  - needs/{i}/focus, which creates a focus_areas row with plan.need and source_need and respects the 409 FOCUS_LIMIT;
  - child_snapshot refresh.
- Observations:
  - add domains[] and attributes;
  - add the details keys when_detail, needs, what_changed, documentation and plan_ref;
  - record_versions on create and PUT;
  - GET filters: date_from, date_to, focus_area_id, domain, context, source;
  - GET /api/observations/{oid}/versions.
- Staff only (staff_child); parents get 404. Audit actions: assessment.create/update/domain_update/close/apply/need_focus.

Frontend:
- features/assessment is the Teacher Observation tab (§5.5): header card, How-to-observe card, 13 domain cards with status pills and 4-tap levels plus notes, Parent-said hints from the profile, D8 binary first, D9 effect chips, D10 play-not-test line, D11 day map, D12 slots, D13 need cards with 'Make it a Current Focus', cycle switcher.
- features/observations turns QuickObservationForm into the A–E stepper, with domain and attribute chips and helper texts.

Implement OM-D15..D17 and D99 plus X-12, X-14, X-17, X-18, X-21, X-23, X-24 and X-25 (§4.3, §5.7, §5.8).

Focus areas:
- add follow_up_on and assessment_id;
- new review_on values must be ISO dates;
- every create, update and status change, including review decisions, writes a record_versions row with via manual or review and review_id, so reopening a goal no longer loses the earlier closure;
- GET ?assessment_id;
- GET /api/focus-areas/{fid}/versions.

Reviews:
- follow_up uses FollowUpIn with improvement_levels and involvement_steps from lists/plan.json, including referral_as_needed labelled per OQ-2;
- the involvement note gets a warning only;
- /suggest now persists an ai_suggestions row through app.ai.service (contract in §7.7; mock it in tests until WP2-AI lands) and returns suggestion_id, possible_patterns and next_observation_questions;
- saving a review records ai_suggestion_id and sets the suggestion outcome.

Functional summaries:
- list, create draft (append-only rows with supersedes_id), suggest (via app.ai.service.draft_functional_summary; inserts an AIS row only) and approve;
- teacher text gets the wording check.

Baselines: GET /api/children/{id}/baselines/{bid} returns the full data, with the first baseline flagged original.

Frontend:
- features/focus becomes the Plan tab (§5.7): 6 editable plan columns plus strength/need/adaptation, the 2–3 goals guidance banner, the Family hopes panel, D13 candidates, closed goals with history, and Export plan via a link to the Reports dialog.
- features/development gains the understanding sequence, the Follow-up review step, the Functional summary card (Write / Draft with AI / Approve, compare with the AI draft, history) and an original-vs-latest baseline viewer.

Implement X-20 (timeline part), X-22 (UI), X-33, X-34 and OM-D99-01 (§5.1, §4.5).

ChildLayout: TabNav with 8 tabs in logical order (Overview · Parent View · Teacher Observation · Plan · Activities · Observations · Development · Reports), using the WP1 path builders. It scrolls on phones and works in RTL. The child header shows the kindergarten and an Export PDF action that links to the Reports tab.

ChildProfilePage becomes the Overview, in the OM-D99-01 order:
- 'From the heart' card: prominent, staff only, PARENT SAID;
- 'Good to know': most important thing, routines, overwhelm, food/medical indicators linking to the Parent View, how to reach the family;
- main strengths ⭐, interests, what helps, current focus with the next review date, recent development;
- prompts: quick baseline, the open question for the family, review-later domains;
- ProvenanceBadge on every chip.

features/observation-history is the Observations tab: a list and detail view over GET /observations with URL-kept filters (date range, focus, domain, context, source) and an edited marker with versions. No charts, counts or percentages.

Timeline: filters in the backend (date_from, date_to, focus_area_id, domain, content_type, result, type[]), with each source filtered before the merge. New entry types: questionnaire_submitted, plan_changed (record_versions focus_area), summary_approved, assessment_closed. focus_closed entries are built from record_versions so reopened goals keep their closures. The Timeline UI becomes a filterable section reachable from the Development tab; the old route redirects.

Implement §7 and X-15, X-19, X-26..X-31 and X-60 (future types documented only).

Context (ai/context.py):
- registry-driven deny-list: health, medical, family and third_party sensitivity, parent free text and identity fields never enter a payload;
- 'avoid' comes only from teacher-observed TA.sensory items whose effect is affects or sometimes;
- baseline_items(for_ai) drops sensitivity support needs;
- plan.who is dropped and observations.note is no longer appended;
- name_masker also scrubs phone numbers and e-mail addresses;
- analysis payloads use the [child] token and the response is restored locally; content generation keeps the first or preferred name (OQ-4).

Domains: new app/ai/domains.py with the relevance map (focus category, strength target or analysis → the 12 AI domains). AIContext.domains is filled only for relevant domains, with caps, from the latest teacher assessment, observations.domains and help keys. The domains used are stored in generation_input or ai_suggestions.domains.

Outputs:
- UnderstandingSuggestion gains possible_patterns and next_observation_questions;
- new FunctionalSummaryDraft schema, prompt and template fallback, with no follow-up-with-parents, involvement, focus-decision or closing fields;
- service functions draft_functional_summary(db, child, lang, user) and suggest_understanding(...) both persist an ai_suggestions row (the contract with WP2-PLAN).

Safety: banned_terms.ai_only is applied to every AI output field; child_deficit terms are also checked on teacher-facing AI text; on violation, fall back to the template provider.

Content:
- record_versions on generate, regenerate and edit;
- DELETE soft-deletes (deleted_at, deleted_by) per OQ-5, and lists hide soft-deleted rows;
- GET /api/content/{cid}/versions;
- the frontend content review shows earlier versions (AI draft vs edits) and the domains used.

New router GET /api/children/{id}/ai-suggestions (staff only).

This is the only package in wave 3, so it may make integration fixes in any file.

Wiring:
- connect WP2-PLAN's suggest and functional-summary calls to the real WP2-AI service functions and remove the mocks;
- point the WP2-PDF builders at the real registries produced by WP2-PQ and WP2-TO;
- check the WP2-NAV links into the WP2-PQ, WP2-TO, WP2-PLAN and WP2-PDF routes.

test_coverage_matrix.py parses every '| PQ-', '| OM-' and '| X-' row of docs/mvp-refocus/COVERAGE-MATRIX.md and checks:
- the IDs equal exactly the union of the registry ids in backend/app/data/source/*.json, plus the X-01..X-64 list;
- each status is one of covered, partial or missing;
- each registry item's storage path resolves to a real Pydantic field (profile section model, assessment domain model, observation details, FollowUpIn, FunctionalSummary) or a real column in app.models;
- the AI column matches the registry ai_policy;
- every registry item with a PDF entry is emitted by its report builder;
- every UI label key exists in en, ar and he.

test_source_docs_e2e.py runs a full flow:
1. A parent fills all 9 steps, including health, and a heart message.
2. A teacher saves the quick baseline (3 strengths) and creates a baseline.
3. The teacher fills 13 domains, marks 2 needs and promotes one to a focus.
4. The teacher plans with all 6 fields, generates content (the payload policy holds) and records feedback.
5. The teacher reviews with follow-up and approves a functional summary.
6. All 6 PDFs are exported in he and ar.
7. History shows the initial versions intact.

After the run:
- update COVERAGE-MATRIX.md statuses to the implemented state and record the OQ answers;
- update ARCHITECTURE.md;
- run the full server CI;
- deploy per deploy/README.md (pg_dump, migrate, restart, smoke test).
